@lang en

IMPORT prelude

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance [New Version] — s 33A, the two definitions that open
-- Part C, Chapter Three. Row IL-01.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt
--   (sha256 b87f2cf4...b81b6; "line N" is a line of that file). Hebrew is
--   authoritative; quotations are rendered mechanically by render_source.py.
--
-- Amounts are new Israeli shekels (NIS), as bare NUMBERs.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE TAKES AS GIVEN, AND WHY. A credit point is written in the
-- section as NIS 504, but the law's figure for any tax year is that amount as
-- indexed every 1 January under s 120B (and frozen for 2025-2027 by
-- s 120B(e)(1)). s 120B belongs to row IL-03 and is not encoded here, so every
-- rule below that needs the year's figure takes it as an input, with no
-- default. The Wikisource editorial notes beside the definitions carry
-- figures (2,820; 2,904; 235; 242); they are not statute text and are never
-- used as values. Official figures, where sourced, are in
-- ito-credit-points-published-figures.l4, labelled as published figures.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Part C, Chapter Three — Deductions, credits and child allowances`
-- line 1559: פרק שלישי: ניכויים, זיכויים וקיצבאות ילדים

§§ `Section 33A — Definitions`
-- line 1561: סעיף 33א: הגדרות
-- line 1562: בפרק זה –
-- "In this Chapter": both definitions below are confined to Part C, Chapter
-- Three (ss 33A-48A). The rules that use them in this encoding are ss 34, 36
-- and 36A, all inside that Chapter, so the confinement changes no answer here.

§§§ `"נקודת זיכוי" — a credit point`
-- line 1563: ”נקודת זיכוי“ – סכום של 504 שקלים חדשים ... לשנת מס, צמוד למדד כאמור בסעיף 120א, המקוזז כנגד המס לאותה שנה;
--
-- Three limbs: (1) an amount, NIS 504, for a tax year; (2) indexed; (3) set
-- off against the tax for that year.
--
-- Wikisource editorial note at the elision, NOT statute text, NOT used:
-- line 1563: (נקוב לשנת 1987; בשנת 2023, 2,820 ש״ח; בשנים 2024–2027, 2,904 ש״ח)

-- Limb (1). The amount as the section writes it, before indexation. A statutory
-- constant; the year's figure is this amount as indexed (limb 2).
@ref ITO s 33A, "נקודת זיכוי", limb (1), line 1563
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of a credit point as written in section 33A, before indexation` MEANS 504

-- Limb (2): "צמוד למדד כאמור בסעיף 120א". Not encoded: see fork F6. The
-- section points at s 120A, whose definition of "מדד" has been deleted; the
-- operative indexation of "סכומי נקודת זיכוי" is s 120B(a) (line 4338), row
-- IL-03. Every rule below takes the indexed figure for the tax year as an
-- input named `the value of one credit point`.

-- A credit point is an amount per point, so a number of points is worth that
-- number times the year's figure. The Israel Tax Authority states the same
-- arithmetic for 2025 (ito-credit-points-published-figures.l4).
@ref ITO s 33A, "נקודת זיכוי", limbs (1)-(2), line 1563
GIVEN `the number of credit points`   IS A NUMBER  @desc a number of credit points, possibly fractional (e.g. 2.25)
      `the value of one credit point` IS A NUMBER  @desc NIS; the s 33A amount as indexed under s 120B for the tax year (2,904 for 2025 per the Israel Tax Authority)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of` `the number of credit points` `credit points at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` MEANS
    `the number of credit points` TIMES `the value of one credit point`

-- Limb (3): "המקוזז כנגד המס לאותה שנה" — set off against the tax for that
-- year. Read (fork F5) as reducing that year's tax, never below zero: a
-- set-off extinguishes no more than the debt it is set against, and "לאותה
-- שנה" ties it to that year, so an excess is neither refunded nor carried to
-- another year. The tax itself comes from s 121 and its neighbours (row
-- IL-03), and the order in which several credits are set off is outside this
-- slice, so both are inputs.
@ref ITO s 33A, "נקודת זיכוי", limb (3), line 1563; fork F5
GIVEN `the credit-point amount` IS A NUMBER  @desc NIS; the number of credit points times the value of one credit point
      `the tax for the year`    IS A NUMBER  @desc NIS; the tax for the tax year before the credit-point amount is set off
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax for the year after setting off` `the credit-point amount` `against` `the tax for the year` MEANS
    max 0 (`the tax for the year` MINUS `the credit-point amount`)

§§§ `"נקודת קיצבה" — an allowance point`
-- line 1564: ”נקודת קיצבה“ – סכום השווה לסכום נקודת זיכוי כערכה ביום כ״א בטבת התשנ״ז (31 בדצמבר 1996), כשהוא מתואם לפי הוראות סעיף 120ב לענין נקודת קיצבה ומחולק בשנים עשר
--
-- Three limbs: (1) the amount of a credit point as it stood on 31 December
-- 1996; (2) adjusted under s 120B "for an allowance point" — s 120B(a) each
-- 1 January and s 120B(b) mid-year on a cost-of-living agreement, row IL-03;
-- (3) divided by twelve. Limbs (1)-(2) produce one figure this row cannot
-- compute, so it is the input; limb (3) is encoded.
--
-- Wikisource editorial note, NOT statute text, NOT used:
-- line 1564: ( בשנת 2023, 235 ש״ח; בשנים 2024–2027, 242 ש״ח)
--
-- The allowance point is consumed by s 40(a) (child allowance points paid by
-- the National Insurance Institute), which is outside this row.
@ref ITO s 33A, "נקודת קיצבה", line 1564
GIVEN `the credit-point value at 31 December 1996, as adjusted under section 120B for an allowance point` IS A NUMBER  @desc NIS; the s 33A credit point as it stood on 31 December 1996, adjusted under s 120B for an allowance point
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of an allowance point, given` `the credit-point value at 31 December 1996, as adjusted under section 120B for an allowance point` MEANS
    `the credit-point value at 31 December 1996, as adjusted under section 120B for an allowance point` DIVIDED BY 12

-- line 1567: ראו סימולטור לחישוב נקודות זיכוי באתר רשות המסים.
-- A Wikisource editorial pointer to the Tax Authority's simulator, after the
-- section. Not law; carried here so the section has no silent gap.
